From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agent OS <agent-os@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996-oneplus: enable q6asm frontends

The OnePlus 3 sound card declares MultiMedia1 through MultiMedia16 DAI
links, but its q6asmdai node only enables DAI IDs 0 through 2. Since the
6.12 q6asm driver registers only DAI children present in device tree, the
sound card parser stops at MultiMedia4 with "error getting cpu dai name" and
no ALSA card is registered.

Enable the remaining q6asm frontend IDs referenced by the existing sound
card. This keeps the existing sound-card links and routes unchanged while
making the card register; the recovery capture and playback paths continue
to use MultiMedia1 and MultiMedia3.

Signed-off-by: Agent OS <agent-os@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-oneplus-common.dtsi | 52 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-oneplus-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-oneplus-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-oneplus-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-oneplus-common.dtsi
@@ -443,6 +443,58 @@
 	dai@2 {
 		reg = <2>;
 	};
+
+	dai@3 {
+		reg = <3>;
+	};
+
+	dai@4 {
+		reg = <4>;
+	};
+
+	dai@5 {
+		reg = <5>;
+	};
+
+	dai@6 {
+		reg = <6>;
+	};
+
+	dai@7 {
+		reg = <7>;
+	};
+
+	dai@8 {
+		reg = <8>;
+	};
+
+	dai@9 {
+		reg = <9>;
+	};
+
+	dai@a {
+		reg = <10>;
+	};
+
+	dai@b {
+		reg = <11>;
+	};
+
+	dai@c {
+		reg = <12>;
+	};
+
+	dai@d {
+		reg = <13>;
+	};
+
+	dai@e {
+		reg = <14>;
+	};
+
+	dai@f {
+		reg = <15>;
+	};
 };
 
 &rpm_requests {
